  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}4{z}^{3}\\,dz]dA & ={\u222c}_{D}{[{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{y}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}({(\\sqrt{y})}^{4}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1-x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}((1-x)^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-x)^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[-\\frac{1}{4}(1-x)^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(0+\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
